same for `case 4:` in the tail switch); the driver's `pat1`/`pat2` byte patterns confirm it.\n- **Stale `temp_key`:** `stbds_hmput_key`'s wrap-around scan sets `temp` but not `temp_key` on a key hit. Kept — the driver's `shputs` test shows both libraries producing the same duplicated keys and the same glibc \"double free detected\" abort (exit 134).\n- `helxo` passes a 16-byte struct by value to `printf(\"%s %c\\n\", ...)`; under SysV the two eightbytes satisfy `%s`/`%c`. Replicated with an explicit `(key, value as c_int)` call — verified identical (`bob h / sally e / fred l / jen l / doug o`).\n- Same libc entry points (`realloc`/`free`/`memcpy`/`memmove`/`strcmp`/`printf`/`sprintf`), same `#[repr(C)]` layouts, same fall-through/goto control flow, same `static` hash-seed evolution, and `STBDS_ASSERT` as a no-op (no assertion fires even in the assertions-enabled C build).\n\nFiles written: `Cargo.toml` (`crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`) and `src/{lib,ffi,hash,array,hashmap,arena,demo}.rs`. Nothing in `c_src/` was modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":516,"cache_read_input_tokens":123613,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":516,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0235f1c5-2d81-4b00-bc67-d6e09faa3980","uuid":"58f6f2e4-817c-45e8-9248-fe5003528291","timestamp":"2026-08-20T03:23:38.182Z"}
